# Dev server restart

After **material** changes to an app under `apps/` (routes, components, services, config that affects runtime), restart that app's dev server in the Dev Container so the user can verify immediately.

## Port map (workspace container)

| App | Port | Restart command (inside container) |
|-----|------|-----------------------------------|
| `apps/api` | **3001** (`API_PORT`) | `npm run start:dev --workspace=apps/api` |
| `apps/admin` | **3000** (`ADMINJS_PORT`) | `npm run start:dev --workspace=apps/admin` |
| `apps/eventguide` | 3002 | `npm run start:dev --workspace=apps/eventguide -- -p 3002` |
| `apps/presentation` | 3003 | `npm run start:dev --workspace=apps/presentation -- -p 3003` |
| `apps/registration` | 3004 | `npm run start:dev --workspace=apps/registration -- -p 3004` |
| `apps/voting` | 3005 | `npm run start:dev --workspace=apps/voting -- -p 3005` |

## How to restart

From the host (container name `coolestproject-dev-workspace`):

```bash
docker exec coolestproject-dev-workspace bash -lc "
  fuser -k <PORT>/tcp 2>/dev/null || pkill -f '<PORT>' || true
  sleep 2
  cd /workspace && nohup npm run start:dev --workspace=apps/<name> -- -p <PORT> > /tmp/<name>.log 2>&1 &
"
```

Then verify with `curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' http://127.0.0.1:<PORT>/`.

Skip restart for test-only, doc-only, or comment-only edits.
